# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Azure AI Speech — Uzbek neural voices (uz-UZ-MadinaNeural / uz-UZ-SardorNeural)
#
# 1. Copy this file:            cp .env.example .env
# 2. Lock it down (Mac/Linux):  chmod 600 .env
# 3. Fill in the values below.  .env is git-ignored — never commit it.
# 4. Check (prints no secrets): npm run check-env
#
# The key is only read by the local Node.js process (generator server / CLI).
# It is never sent to the browser and never written to logs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Azure portal → your Speech resource → "Keys and Endpoint" → KEY 1.
# In a Claude Code cloud session the real key is stored as a network secret instead
# (see README) — then leave this placeholder as it is; the proxy fills in the real key.
AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=your-azure-speech-key

# Same page → "Location/Region", lower-case without spaces, e.g. westeurope, eastus.
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=westeurope

# Optional: port of the generator web page (default 3333).
# GENERATOR_PORT=3333

# Optional: existing Chrome/Chromium for rendering (only needed when Remotion
# cannot download its own browser).
# REMOTION_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE=/path/to/chrome-headless-shell
